# Navigation disarm, tag library context commit: clear the M3U
# staging flag when module 24 commits a new library play context.
name: nav-tag-disarm
kind: module
module: 24
region: code
address: 0x0307ec72
gate: build refuses unless the 4 stock bytes at the target equal
  `expect`. Do NOT stack without the module 24 segment extension
  (--grow 24:code: with tag24.bin) carrying the stub at the branch
  target 0x0307EDEC, the first byte past module 24's stock code.
expect: a5f8f2c0
replace: 00f0bbb8
rationale: Module 24 constructs the play context for a selected
  library list; at this site it stores the category from
  0x030235C0 into the play context at +0xF2 (strh.w ip, [r5, #0xF2]).
  The stub clears the staging flag byte at 0x0307BFB4, reproduces
  the displaced store and returns to 0x0307EC76. A same-track
  branch returns earlier and never reaches the site, so resuming
  the same track does not disarm. Source:
  patches/navigation/tag_exit.S, proven by
  patches/navigation/test_tag_exit.py (ten category values, both
  flag states) and re-proven at this placement by the full build's
  lifecycle audit.
